== D. mixed technologies (T1.8): e_g = -(1-b_L)/(1-a_L), e_u = +(1-b_m)/(1-a_L) ==
 prec level / reset members: e_g = -theta - 1;  e_u = (alpha*theta + alpha - 1)/alpha
 reset level / prec members: e_g = -1;  e_u = alpha*(theta + 1)/(alpha*theta + alpha - 1)

== E. same-alpha premise (analytic note, numerics in c2 mixed rows and c5) ==
 Flat member's marginal error from adding S_g: (1/pi) Int S_g(w) r/(r+S_u(w)) dw; near w->0 the integrand ~ q_g r w^(alpha_u-alpha_g)/q_u,
 finite iff alpha_g - alpha_u < 1. Then the flat gain is linear in q_g and d ln N*/d ln q_g -> -(1+theta) at fixed q_u;
 at alpha_g - alpha_u >= 1 the gain is sub-linear in q_g and the exponent changes (c5).
